# Build context exclusions (Bab 37 rule 2 follow-up, found during the
# multi-stage Dockerfile rebuild+verify pass) — this file didn't exist
# before, so `COPY . .` was baking the host's venv/ (338MB, redundant — the
# image builds its own), web/node_modules/ (277MB, irrelevant to the Python
# backend), and — the real finding — the literal `.env` file (with live
# provider API keys) directly into every image layer. `docker-compose.yml`
# already injects `.env` at runtime via `env_file:`; it must never also be
# copied into the image filesystem itself.

# Secrets — never bake real credentials into image layers.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Python
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Runtime data/logs — volume-mounted (reports/uploads) or regenerated fresh
# in the container; baking in stale copies wastes space and can shadow the
# mount depending on build vs. mount order.
audit.log
security_audit.log
*.log
uploads/
reports/

# Frontend — api/main.py serves the already-built web/dist/ output; the
# Python image has no use for node_modules or frontend source/tests.
web/node_modules/
web/src/
web/tests/
web/node_modules
web/.vite/

# VCS / tooling / docs — not needed by the running app.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.idea/
.vscode/
docs/
k8s/
backups/
*.swp
.DS_Store
